# Fix: Members disappearing after Render deploy

Problem: You had members, after push and Render update, only 1 member shows.
Cause: Render free tier file system is ephemeral. data/members.json committed in git overwrites live data on deploy. Also `[]` Out-File commands overwrite real members locally.

Fix in this app_FIXED_MEMBERS_PERSISTENT.py:
1. DATA_DIR = os.environ.get('DATA_DIR', 'data') - uses persistent disk if set
2. load_json_preserve() - never overwrites existing members.json with [] if file exists and has data. Copies from fallback data/ if persistent disk empty.
3. All data files use DATA_DIR, ensured exist without overwriting.
4. .gitignore for data/*.json - prevents pushing local empty files over real members on Render.

Render setup (do once):
- Dashboard -> your service -> Disks -> Add Disk
  Name: chapel-data
  Mount Path: /opt/render/project/src/data
  Size: 1GB (free tier allows)
  Save, Render will redeploy and keep data/ persistent.

Local setup (don't lose members):
- Never run `[] | Out-File data/members.json` - that deletes all members
- Only run for new files: member_events, galleries, videos, online, chats, notifications if they don't exist
- Add data/members.json to .gitignore so your local push doesn't overwrite Render's real members

Recovery if you lost members:
- Check Render -> Shell -> cat data/members.json
- If empty, restore from backup: Render dashboard -> manual backup or local backup
- Or re-approve from pending registrations in data/members.json.bak if exists

This fix preserves all achievements: organized by media type, online, chat, like, comment, auto-appear, church+member events.
